**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `DELETE_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ProjectJsonRoundtripTests -> OpticalConstructor.Tests.TableViewTests`

**How to implement.** The project codec, its schema and the aggregate record go (001 §R '`.ocproj`: … the `ProjectJson` project aggregate and the `Project` record. Kits replace them, and the JSON + schema stack is reused (§B)'; the S4.4 brief: the serializer options already live in the canonical-JSON module, step 21, so `ProjectJson.fs` goes whole). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs` (`ProjectJson.fs:ProjectJson`: `schemaVersion`, `ProjectJsonText` with `value` and `parseProject`, `serializeProject`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:23`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs`: `projectSchemaFile`, the project-schema lazy and `validate` (`SchemaValidation.fs:31-36` and `:61-76` in today's tree; `validate` answers `validateWith` over the project schema since step 29) are deleted; `tryLoadSchema`, `collectMessages`, `validateWith` and the per-kind validators stay. The module doc (`:9-12`) becomes one to three lines naming no project. (3) `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json` is deleted with its `Content` item (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:58-60`). The one live reader of it moves with what it reads: the material file's `materialEntry` check (`Report.fs:materialEntrySchema`, which wraps the project schema's `$defs` today). New `schema/material-metadata.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 with `$id` `https://berreman/schema/material-metadata.json`, root `"$ref": "#/$defs/materialEntry"`, and `$defs` holding `materialEntry`, `dispersionModel`, `thermoOptic` and `unitOfMeasure` exactly as the project schema holds them (they are `materialEntry`'s whole reference closure), is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` in the project schema's place. In `Report.fs`, `materialEntrySchema` becomes the lazy `tryLoadSchema` of that file (`SchemaValidation.fs:tryLoadSchema`, through a private `FileName` bound once, as `projectSchemaFile` was) and `validateEntryElement` answers `validateWith materialEntrySchema element` (step 29's one evaluation body), so its refusal carries the evaluation's messages. The `MaterialLibrary` module doc and `materialEntrySchema`'s doc each become one to three lines naming the new file and no project schema. `importMaterials`, `exportMaterials` and the DTO are otherwise unchanged. (4) Domain: `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Project.fs` (`Project.fs:Project`: `OpticalConstructorProject`, `schemaDefAnchors`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj:42`); the comment above `Groups.fs`'s `<Compile>` (`:43-45`) loses 'compiles after Project'. `BeamTree`, `SourceSpec`, `Placement` and `Table` stay: other code uses them. (5) Docs that name the record: `Sidecar.fs`'s module doc (`Sidecar.fs:12-14`) and `SidecarTests.fs`'s (`SidecarTests.fs:14-15`) lose the sentence about the canonical project; every comment in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj` that names `ProjectJson` is cut to the words that stay true. Sidecar itself is unchanged. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ProjectJsonRoundtripTests.fs` is deleted with its `<Compile>` line: `AC-C1 a fresh project table is 1.2 x 2.0 x 0.10 m` moves unchanged into `TableViewTests`, with any open it needs, and the other facts go with the codec (`AC-A2 a valid canonical project validates on load`, `AC-D6 round-trip preserves the defaultUnit label and the canonical SI datum`, `AC-A5 the canonical SI magnitudes are stored verbatim`, `AC-B9 beam tree and systems round-trip through the schema-validated canonical project`, `AC-B9 the filled beamNode $def rejects a malformed incident shape on load`, `AC-C1 the edited table size round-trips through the schema-validated canonical project`). In `PlacementTests.fs`, `AC-A6 a project carrying placement round-trips through the canonical JSON and passes schema validation` is deleted with the fixtures only it used (`PlacementTests.fs:149-175`: `vacuumSystem`, `light`, `rootNode`, `okOr`) and the opens left unused (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.Errors` and any other); the module doc drops its AC-A6 clause. A placement's round trip is held for kit files by `SceneRoundTripTests`' `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state` (step 148). `StackEditTests.fs` loses `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project` (`StackEditTests.fs:11`), which names nothing it uses. `ExportImportTests` gains `a material entry outside the materialEntry definition is SchemaValidationErr`: `validateEntryElement` of an element whose `category` is `NotACategory` (with a GUID `id` and a `name`) answers `Error (SchemaValidationErr messages)` with `messages` not empty. (7) The record's census also names `History.fs` (deleted at step 158), `ProjectFile.fs` and `RoundTripTests.fs` (deleted at step 159), and `RecentFiles.fs` and `HistoryTests.fs` (emptied of it at step 159); they are in scope only so the retirement covers its whole census, and nothing more changes in them. Afterwards `git grep -n -E "ProjectJson|OpticalConstructorProject|schemaDefAnchors|optical-constructor-project|Domain.Project" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the codec, the project schema and the record are deleted, `git grep -n -E "ProjectJson|OpticalConstructorProject|schemaDefAnchors|optical-constructor-project|Domain.Project" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing, and `MaterialLibrary.validateEntryElement` MUST validate against `schema/material-metadata.schema.json`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a material entry outside the materialEntry definition is SchemaValidationErr`, `AC-C1 a fresh project table is 1.2 x 2.0 x 0.10 m` under TableViewTests and every other ExportImportTests fact, the count falling by 6; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.
